## The honest summary, plain language

**The bad news first (no yes-man):** there is **no ready-made Bulgarian humanizer anywhere in open source.** The famous repos are English (blader/humanizer, 50k★), Chinese, Korean, and one Russian (humanizer-ru — the only Cyrillic one, but Russian ≠ Bulgarian). The two tools with real peer-reviewed evasion results (DIPPER, TempParaphraser) only work on English and need heavy GPUs. Anyone claiming a "Bulgarian AI humanizer" is lying.

**But the weapons we need are buildable TODAY on what we already have — OpenRouter at $0.01–0.10/paper.** My top 3, ranked:

1. **Translation-chain pipeline** (lynote-ai/humanize-text, MIT, 3k★) — rewrite at high temperature → push text through distant languages (Finnish/German) → rebuild in Bulgarian. Its config **natively supports OpenRouter** — I verified it in their actual config file. This is the mechanism with the strongest evidence: DIPPER's paper (abstract verified live) shows controlled paraphrasing crashed DetectGPT from 70.3% → 4.6%.
2. **A Bulgarian "de-AI" skill** — fork the 50k★ humanizer's 25 tell-patterns + the academic-humanizer's 6 layers, swap in Bulgarian tells (канцелярит, "в съвременния свят", forced triads, uniform rhythm). The Russian tool proves this works on Cyrillic and documents why English patterns *fail* on it.
3. **A detector-informed loop** — score your paragraph → minimally rewrite only the riskiest sentences → re-check with free GPTZero + a local detector (desklib/ai-text-detector-academic-v1.01). Never claim "clean" without a before/after measurement. Its rules protect citations/numbers — which is your academic survival condition anyway.

**What the evidence says about mechanisms (with numbers):** adversarial paraphrasing cuts detector TPR by 87.88% (NeurIPS 2025); style humanization hits 92% attack success; raising perplexity works because human text scores 29.5 vs LLM's 15.2; **but** surface-only fixes plateau (95.5→93.9 in the StoryScope study) — you must fix structure and rhythm, not just words. And Slavic is genuinely advantageous: the best Russian detector only hits 86.35% on a 52K-text benchmark, and **no Bulgarian benchmark has ever been published.**

**Bottom line:** buy the pipeline, build the BG patterns, close the measurement loop. First test: 3 generated Bulgarian papers through Rank 1 + Rank 3 with before/after GPTZero scores. That's a real system — not a hope.
